        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-72" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;rounded=0;" value="Document&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;(Text Chunk)&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="120" x="810" y="310" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-77" edge="1" parent="1" source="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-73" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-76" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-73" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;rounded=0;" value="Retrieved documents + User query" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="140" x="1015" y="310" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-79" edge="1" parent="1" source="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-76" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-78" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-76" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;rounded=0;" value="LLM Model" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="120" x="1240" y="310" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-78" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;rounded=0;" value="Output (Response)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="120" x="1440" y="310" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-80" parent="1" style="shape=callout;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;perimeter=calloutPerimeter;base=15;" value="&lt;p&gt;Augmented Genration -&amp;gt; We pass the retrieved documents, along with the initial user query, to the LLM to generate the response.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="90" width="310" x="940" y="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-85" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fillStyle=solid;direction=west;gradientDirection=north;shadow=1;size=0;autosizeText=1;fontSize=7;align=left;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Scenario&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;You are a developer at a company called Antech, and your tech lead asks you to build a chatbot to help internal employees with their day-to-day questions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;These questions are company-specific, and the information is not available on the internet. The company has a collection of manuals that help employees handle common situations they may encounter in their daily work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Those manuals are very extensive, and new employees are complaining about the amount of time it takes to read all the necessary information before they can start working at the company.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;You have to build a solution to make this information easier and more natural to consume.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="390" x="-730" y="-540" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-88" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fillStyle=solid;direction=west;gradientDirection=north;shadow=1;size=0;autosizeText=1;fontSize=6;align=left;" value="&lt;h3&gt;Main Problems&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. The information isn&#39;t available on the internet.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This means that no matter which LLM we choose, it won&#39;t have access to the company&#39;s specific information needed to answer employees&#39; questions about their daily work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;LLMs are mainly trained on publicly available information, so they won&#39;t necessarily have access to private company knowledge.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. The manuals are very extensive.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;LLMs have a limited context window, so we can&#39;t simply send the entire manual with every employee question.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;That would be very expensive in terms of tokens, and providing too much irrelevant context could also negatively affect the quality of the model&#39;s response.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;The Problem&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Specific information that the model doesn&#39;t have in its training data + a large amount of contextual information.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;These are exactly the kinds of problems that RAG can help us solve.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="320" x="-70" y="-540" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-89" edge="1" parent="1" source="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-85" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-88">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="50" y="-460" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-91" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fillStyle=solid;direction=west;gradientDirection=north;shadow=1;size=0;autosizeText=1;fontSize=6;align=left;" value="&lt;h2&gt;RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;In a RAG architecture, we have two main phases:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h2&gt;1. Ingestion Phase&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;We process the documents and transform their content into embeddings using an embedding model. These embeddings are then stored in a vector database, which acts as our knowledge base.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;This knowledge base will be used during the retrieval phase when a user asks a question.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h2&gt;2. Retrieval Phase&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;When a user asks a question, the query is transformed into an embedding, which is then used to perform a similarity search in the vector database.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;The search returns the top-K most similar document chunks.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;These retrieved documents are then passed to the LLM along with the original user query to provide the context needed to generate the response.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="235" width="510" x="470" y="-570" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-102" edge="1" parent="1" source="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-96" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" target="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-101">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-96" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fillStyle=solid;direction=west;gradientDirection=north;shadow=1;size=0;autosizeText=1;fontSize=6;align=left;" value="&lt;h3&gt;Problems We Solve&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Grounded responses&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;The chatbot&#39;s responses are grounded in the information retrieved from our knowledge base.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Instead of relying only on the LLM&#39;s internal knowledge, we provide it with relevant document chunks containing real company information to help generate the response.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Reduced token usage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;We don&#39;t need to pass the entire knowledge base to the LLM with every question.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Instead, we perform a similarity search based on the user&#39;s query and retrieve only the most relevant pieces of information to provide as context to the LLM.&lt;/p&gt; " vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="125" width="330" x="1250" y="-515" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-97" edge="1" parent="1" source="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-88" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;entryX=0;entryY=0;entryDx=510;entryDy=125;entryPerimeter=0;" target="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-91">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-99" edge="1" parent="1" source="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-91" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;entryX=0;entryY=0;entryDx=330;entryDy=62.5;entryPerimeter=0;" target="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-96">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-100" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fillStyle=solid;direction=west;gradientDirection=north;shadow=1;size=0;autosizeText=1;fontSize=7;align=left;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Embedding — Quick Explanation&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;An embedding is a numerical representation of data, such as text.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;An embedding model converts text into a vector of numbers that captures its semantic meaning.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&quot;How can I reset my password?&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;becomes something like:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;[0.12, -0.45, 0.78, 0.03, ...]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Texts with similar meanings tend to have similar vectors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In RAG, we use these vectors to find the most relevant documents or chunks for a user&#39;s query.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="335" x="-670" y="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="utXbo1NHayFTNu2cgIt0-101" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fillStyle=solid;direction=west;gradientDirection=north;shadow=1;size=0;autosizeText=1;fontSize=6;align=left;" value="&lt;h3&gt;What Naive RAG Doesn&#39;t Solve&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Naive RAG is a good starting point, but it has some important limitations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;First, &lt;strong&gt;retrieval quality&lt;/strong&gt;. If we retrieve the wrong chunks, the LLM will receive the wrong context and may generate an incorrect answer.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Second, &lt;strong&gt;poor chunking&lt;/strong&gt;. If our chunks are too small, we may lose important context. If they are too large, we may retrieve too much irrelevant information.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Third, &lt;strong&gt;query complexity&lt;/strong&gt;. A user&#39;s question may be ambiguous, poorly formulated, or contain multiple questions. A simple vector search may not be enough to understand what the user actually needs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;And finally, &lt;strong&gt;relevance&lt;/strong&gt;. The most semantically similar chunks are not always the most relevant ones for answering the question.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;So, while Naive RAG gives us the basic pipeline, it doesn&#39;t solve the entire retrieval problem.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;And this is where &lt;strong&gt;Advanced RAG techniques&lt;/strong&gt; come in. (Next Videos)&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="360" x="1860" y="-532.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
